# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites files to
# CRLF on the way out, while .prettierrc demands `endOfLine: "lf"` — so any
# file that arrives by checkout rather than by being written locally fails
# `pnpm format:check` on Windows and passes it in CI on Linux. A gate that
# disagrees with itself between machines is worse than no gate: it trains
# whoever sees the red to ignore it.
#
# `eol=lf` (not just `text=auto`) is the load-bearing part — it overrides
# core.autocrlf for the working tree, which is exactly the setting that caused
# the divergence.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary and generated artifacts git must not touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated
